# Anchored: only the built binary at the repo root.  A bare `elps`
# pattern matches ANY path component named elps -- including
# cmd/elpsvet/testdata/src/github.com/luthersystems/elps/..., which
# silently kept new analysistest stub packages out of the repository
# (they existed locally, so tests passed locally and failed in CI).
/elps
# The benchgate binary, when `go build ./cmd/benchgate` is run from the repo
# root. Anchored like /elps above so it cannot match cmd/benchgate/ itself.
/benchgate
.firecrawl/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.tmp/
node_modules/
*.vsix
editors/vscode/dist/
editors/vscode/bin/
.vscode/
.env

# scripts/fuzz.sh collects genuinely-new crashers here so CI can upload those
# rather than the whole committed corpus. Regenerated per run; never committed
# (the crasher itself belongs in <package>/testdata/fuzz/<Target>/).
fuzz-crashers/

# scripts/ci-gates-test.sh synthesises a throwaway package here for its
# empty-discovery control and deletes it again. Ignored so an interrupted run
# cannot leave the tree looking dirty.
internal/citest-emptyfuzz.*/

# `go test -c` / -memprofile leave a compiled test binary beside the package
*.test
